{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>לא ירפך.</b> From holding you fast with His hands. And the expression לֹא יַרְפְּךָ is in the causative — He will not give you slackness, will not separate you from Himself. And likewise ״אֲחַזְתִּיו וְלֹא אַרְפֶּנּוּ״ (Song of Songs 3) — that אֶרְפֶּנּוּ is not pointed [as causative]; every expression of רִפְיוֹן revolves around the causative and reflexive [stems], as in ״הַרְפֵּה לָהּ״ (II Kings 4) — give her slackness; ״הֶרֶף מִמֶּנִּי״ (Deuteronomy 9) — slacken yourself from me."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:01.025073770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}